/*****************************************************************************
    fixBisect -- F-31's bisect. HOW MANY INSTALLS DOES IT TAKE TO POISON THE
    COMPILE OF THE FIRST BODY.

    walkPhase generates 56 bodies and then every one of them fails to compile
    with the identical signature, reached end of input on line 1. compileProbe
    compiles a single body on the same binary and passes, and NamE compiled
    clean standalone. So a body that compiles alone fails once the others are
    installed, and the question is how many others it takes.

    This installs the first fbLimit bodies and then compiles the FIRST one, the
    one that was known good when it was alone. fbLimit is the knob and the
    shell drives it.

    THE DETECTOR IS THE ERROR LINE, NOT compile's RETURN. F-24 records that
    compile returns the field for an uncoded subject, so its return cannot tell
    compiled from never coded. ERROR processCode on stderr is the independent
    signal and the one walkPhase's own count was corroborated against.

    THE GENERATOR IS walkPhase's, COPIED VERBATIM rather than written afresh, so
    a difference between the two fixtures cannot be a difference in what they
    generate.

    ONE SENTINEL, INSIDE THE DRIVER, because installing bodies poisons the
    loader and a driver that returns to it never arrives.

    ⚠⚠ THE ANSWER, 2026-08-19. ONE INSTALL FLIPS IT, AND IT IS THE 43rd:

        fbLimit 42   last installed break      BasicElse fails on CONTENT --
                                               failed at "else() AND followedBy()"
                                               so the body text is READ
        fbLimit 43   last installed tokenize   BasicElse fails at
                                               "reached end of input" on line 1

    Same first body, same compile, one extra install between them. So this is
    not a count and not an accumulation: a single install turns a readable body
    into an empty read, which is the signature all 56 of walkPhase's failures
    carry.

    ⚠ AND N=1 IS NOT THE BUG, WHICH IS WHY THE DETECTOR IS THE SIGNATURE AND NOT
    THE ERROR. BasicElse fails to compile at EVERY N, because its generated body
    calls `else()` and `else` is a keyword -- a real defect but a different one.
    Counting `ERROR processCode` would have reported failure at N=1 and hidden
    the transition entirely. Only "reached end of input" moves.

    ⚠ THE NAME-SKIP CONTROL IS VOID, NOT NEGATIVE, and it is reported as void.
    Two spellings were tried to skip the suspect by name -- `taG eq "tokenize"`
    and `fbCur.taG eq "tokenize"` -- and BOTH matched every member, installing
    nothing at all. A control that installs zero bodies cannot say whether
    skipping one of them mattered. What stands is the A/B above, which isolates
    the same single install without naming it.

    Footnote: docs/fixIts.md F-31.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;
register(FixBisect);
define
    fbBuffer buffer;
    fbOpen="{";
    fbClose="}";
    fbLimit=43;
    fbCount=0;
    fbTermN=0;
    fbFirst;
    fbBump code={
        fbTermN = fbTermN + 1;
        };
    fbTagMatch argument code={
        print $"m" taG;
        print $"()";
        print ";";
        };
    fbGen argument code={
        reset(fbBuffer);
        printTO(fbBuffer);
        print fbOpen:;
        if datA != 0;
            printTO(0);
            return;
        if hasAttributeS;   fbJoin = "AND";
        else                fbJoin = "OR";
        print `"if ";
        fbTermN = 0;
        iterate fbTerm on *argument;
        while ++fbTerm;
            fbBump();
            print $"t" fbTermN "()";
            if nexT;    print _fbJoin;
            else        print ";";
        @argument;
        if fbTermN == 0;    fbTagMatch(argument);
        print $"return runRuleAction(this);":;
        print `fbClose:;
        clear(CodE);
        CodE = fbBuffer;
        fbCopy <- copyOf(CodE);
        fbCopy :. noPrinT;
        argument +% fbCopy;
        argument :. isCodeD;
        printTO(0);
        fbCount = fbCount + 1;
        if fbCount == 1;    fbFirst +% argument;
        cerr "INSTALL " fbCount " " ~taG:;
        };
    fbWalk argument code={
        iterate fbCur members on *argument;
        while ++fbCur;
            if fbCount >= fbLimit;  continue;
            if noPrinT;             continue;
            if binTypE;             continue;
            if !isRulE;             continue;
            if actionTypE != 0;     continue;
            fbGen(fbCur);
        };
    fbRun code={
        fbWalk(Grokking);
        cerr "== installed " fbCount " bodies, now compiling the FIRST ==":;
        iterate fbC on fbFirst;
        while ++fbC;
            cerr "COMPILING " ~taG:;
            compile(fbC);
        cerr "FIXBISECT SENTINEL -- reached the end":;
        stop();
        };
    ;
fbRun();
